IFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905796062","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=905796062","retrieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27:29.718Z","effective_date":"2022-03-22","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1048389-i20211203","date":"2021-12-03","inspection_type":"Inspection","result":"No deficiencies cited","passed":true,"violation_count":0,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905796061","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=905796061","retrieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27:29.718Z","effective_date":"2021-12-03","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1048389-i20211020","date":"2021-10-20","inspection_type":"Investigation of a report","result":"Deficiencies cited","passed":false,"violation_count":8,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905922112","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=905922112","retrieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27:29.718Z","effective_date":"2021-10-20","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[{"id":"tx-hhsc-1048389-i20211020-v1","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-747-2703-4-d","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1048389-i20211020","date":"2021-10-20","original_code":"747.2703(4)(D)","severity":"medium","severity_label":"Medium risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2021-12-03","finding":"Positive Methods of Discipline and Guidance - Brief Supervised Separation: An assistant caregiver placed a crying child in time out in a play yard for 6 minutes. The primary caregiver then moved the play yard with the child inside of it to a bedroom. The child was alone in the bedroom with the door shut for 9 minutes. This was observed through video obtained during the investigation.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026686147","violation_type_title":"Positive Methods of Discipline and Guidance - Brief Supervised Separation (26 TAC §747.2703(4)(D))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1048389-i20211020-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-747-3307-d","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1048389-i20211020","date":"2021-10-20","original_code":"747.3307(d)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2021-12-03","finding":"Diapering Procedures- Sanitizing the Diapering Area: The primary caregiver did not sanitize the diapering surface or use a clean disposable covering in between each diaper change. This was observed through video obtained during the course of the investigation.","topic":"sanitation","source_record_id":"1026678803","violation_type_title":"Diapering Procedures- Sanitizing the Diapering Area (26 TAC §747.3307(d))","topic_label":"Sanitation & hygiene"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1048389-i20211020-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-747-1501-c-1","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1048389-i20211020","date":"2021-10-20","original_code":"747.1501(c)(1)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2021-12-03","finding":"Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Competency, Good Judgment, Self-control: -A caregiver did not use good judgement when placing two infants on top of a table, in bouncer seats when feeding them. This was observed through video obtained during the course of the investigation.   -A caregiver did not use good judgment when picking up a child up by the wrists and placing them inside of a play yard. This was observed through video obtained during the course of the investigation","topic":"staffing","source_record_id":"1026683186","violation_type_title":"Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Competency, Good Judgment, Self-control (26 TAC §747.1501(c)(1))","topic_label":"Staff qualifications & clearances"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1048389-i20211020-v4","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-747-207-4","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1048389-i20211020","date":"2021-10-20","original_code":"747.207(4)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2021-12-03","finding":"Reporting Suspected Abuse, Neglect and Exploitation: The primary caregiver did not report suspected abuse of a child in care. The primary caregiver noted serious concerns regarding bruises that were observed on a child in care and stated that she knew she was required to report the suspected abuse. This information was obtained through the course of the investigation.","topic":"facilities","source_record_id":"1026682319","violation_type_title":"Reporting Suspected Abuse, Neglect and Exploitation (26 TAC §747.207(4))","topic_label":"Facilities & equipment"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1048389-i20211020-v5","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-747-2705-6","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1048389-i20211020","date":"2021-10-20","original_code":"747.2705(6)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2021-12-03","finding":"Prohibited Punishments - Humiliating, Rejecting, Yelling: The primary caregiver yelled into a crying toddler?s face while the child was standing in a play yard. The child fell back into the play yard after the caregiver yelled at them. The primary caregiver then yelled at the child and told them they would not eat if they did not stop crying. After removing the child from the play yard, the primary caregiver told them they would go back in the room if they did not stop crying. This was observed through video obtained during the course of the investigation","topic":"facilities","source_record_id":"1026692001","violation_type_title":"Prohibited Punishments - Humiliating, Rejecting, Yelling (26 TAC §747.2705(6))","topic_label":"Facilities & equipment"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1048389-i20211020-v6","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-747-2307","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1048389-i20211020","date":"2021-10-20","original_code":"747.2307","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2021-12-03","finding":"Infant Care Area Furnishings and Equipment - Use of Safety Straps: A caregiver was observed placing infants in highchairs without using the safety straps. This was observed through video obtained during the course of the investigation.","topic":"facilities","source_record_id":"1026682430","violation_type_title":"Infant Care Area Furnishings and Equipment - Use of Safety Straps (26 TAC §747.2307)","topic_label":"Facilities & equipment"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1048389-i20211020-v7","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-747-2319-1","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1048389-i20211020","date":"2021-10-20","original_code":"747.2319(1)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2021-12-03","finding":"Requirements for Feeding Infants - Hold if Unable to Sit: Two infants, that were not able to sit unassisted, were observed to be fed in bouncer seats. They were not being held by the caregiver as required. This was observed through video obtained during the course of the investigation.","topic":"food","source_record_id":"1026682313","violation_type_title":"Requirements for Feeding Infants - Hold if Unable to Sit (26 TAC §747.2319(1))","topic_label":"Food & nutrition"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1048389-i20211020-v8","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-747-207-10","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1048389-i20211020","date":"2021-10-20","original_code":"747.207(10)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2021-12-03","finding":"AP Never exceed capacity of the home: The daycare home was operating over capacity. A video was provided as part of the investigation and there were at least 13 children observed to be in care.  Thirteen children can clearly be seen in the video and it is unclear if a fourteenth child is laying in a bouncer, on the floor, near the table.","topic":"facilities","source_record_id":"1026691745","violation_type_title":"AP Never exceed capacity of the home (26 TAC §747.207(10))","topic_label":"Facilities & equipment"}]}],"geo":{"state":{"code":"TX","name":"Texas"},"county":{"fips":"48121","name":"Denton County"},"zip":"75007","city":"Carrollton"},"related":{"same_operator":[],"same_operator_total":0,"same_building":[],"same_address_other_authority":[],"nearby":[]}}
